---
/**
 * THE MODEL PAGE STATUS LINE: reviewed date, and the launch year.
 *
 * WHY IT IS A COMPONENT. Antonio asked for the launch year on every equipment
 * page, so DJs can tell how old a unit is and whether they are looking at a
 * current model or something they will only meet in a rental inventory. That is
 * one sentence on 21 models in 3 languages, which is 63 places. Written by hand
 * that is 63 chances to forget one, and today alone produced three separate bugs
 * of exactly that shape: the photo box copied into 57 pages and omitted on the
 * 58th, the h1 rules omitted on six, and a "coming soon" card left on a brand that
 * had gone live. So it is a component and there is nothing to remember.
 *
 * THE YEAR COMES FROM THE EQUIPMENT GRAPH, never from prose. Every model in
 * facts.js carries `released`, so no page can state a year the data layer does not
 * hold, and there is nothing here to invent. A model with no year renders the
 * reviewed date alone rather than an empty label.
 *
 * WHY THE YEAR AND NOT THE FULL DATE. Several constants carry a precise
 * announcement date, and a few of those are announcement rather than availability,
 * which are different events and not comparable across 21 models. A year is the
 * claim that is true for all of them and is what actually answers the reader's
 * question, which is "how old is this".
 */
import { equipmentFor } from '../data/facts.js';
import { UI } from '../i18n/ui.js';

interface Props {
  slug: string;
  checked: string;
  lang?: 'en' | 'pt' | 'es';
}
const { slug, checked, lang = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const S = UI[lang].modelStatus;
const released = equipmentFor(slug)?.released ?? null;
---
<div class="status-line sl-date">
  {S.reviewed}: {checked}
  {released && (
    <>
      <span class="ms-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <span class="ms-launch">{S.launched} {released}</span>
    </>
  )}
</div>

<style>
  /* Inherits .status-line and .sl-date from global.css, so the reviewed date
     renders exactly as it did before this component existed. Only the separator
     and the launch span are new, and both are deliberately quiet: this is
     context, not a headline. */
  .ms-sep { margin: 0 0.45rem; opacity: 0.5; }
  .ms-launch { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
